<section>
  <grid spacing="none">
    <grid-item colspan="39" vertical-align="center">
      <h2>The stay has a missing middle</h2>
      <p>A boutique-hotel journey can move quickly from transport and check-in to dinner plans, work, or sightseeing. The overlooked opportunity is the transition between arriving at the property and feeling present within it.</p>
      <smart-layout orientation="vertical" variant="minimalTimeline">
        <smart-layout-item>
          <h4>Arrive</h4>
          <p font-size="sm">Bags, logistics, notifications, and unfamiliar surroundings compete for attention.</p>
        </smart-layout-item>
        <smart-layout-item>
          <h4>Reset</h4>
          <p font-size="sm">A hosted ritual creates a clear pause and introduces the hotel’s way of caring.</p>
        </smart-layout-item>
        <smart-layout-item>
          <h4>Return</h4>
          <p font-size="sm">The guest continues with an experience to describe, repeat, or add to a future booking.</p>
        </smart-layout-item>
      </smart-layout>
      <p role="caption">Hospitality wellness, not a medical intervention: the value begins with thoughtful time, place, and attention.</p>
    </grid-item>
    <grid-item colspan="21" padding="0">
      <ai-image prompt="Observed editorial hospitality photograph of an adult guest arriving in a boutique hotel room, partial figure by the window setting a phone and travel bag down beside a glass of water, natural afternoon light, tactile white linens, sea-glass accents and deep teal detail, quiet unstaged atmosphere, no text or logos" image-style="restorative-hospitality-editorial" aspect-ratio="portrait" fill="true"/>
    </grid-item>
  </grid>
</section>